and are very restrictive. Activists there have found a new way to help women wanting to terminate a pregnancy: the "Abortomat," a locker that dispenses abortion pills. But they face fierce opposition.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>ASEAN offers Myanmar's sidelined leaders a path back to summits, but says restrictions will stay until there is meaningful progress on its peace plan</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ec35e1688cba912faa4118f93417fbed37cd5b5270e78014452a459307b12515</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:39Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T12:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/asean-offers-myanmar-s-sidelined-leaders-a-path-back-to-summits-but-says-restrictions-will-stay-unti/a-79951878--8a50f9fda2bd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/asean-offers-myanmar-s-sidelined-leaders-a-path-back-to-summits-but-says-restrictions-will-stay-until-there-is-meaningful-progress-on-its-peace-plan/a-79951878?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Southeast Asian leaders have agreed to engage Myanmar in stages after years of excluding its leaders from high-level meetings. The bloc says Myanmar could regain full representation if it makes progress on a peace plan.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria's upcoming election marred by rising AI disinformation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:40af4db108b6b605271dff8f8ab94167e7908876d3c506bd7a99ab94b58262e5</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:39Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T21:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nigeria-s-upcoming-election-marred-by-rising-ai-disinformation/a-79946897--e1618bd315dd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nigeria-s-upcoming-election-marred-by-rising-ai-disinformation/a-79946897?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Nigeria inches closer to the 2027 polls, the use of artificial intelligence 